        {
          "id": 2060348869,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The script that generates the dissector uses `git describe --tags` to add a comment about from which commit was last used to regenerate, where \"N commits since tag X\" is part of the description (in a machine friendly format.) It doesn't work right if the history doesn't include the last tag.\n\nWe could add a note about that, or possibly change the versioning text so it doesn't need a tag.\n\nSadly git doesn't make it easy to say \"fetch all the history up to the most recent tag.\" It's a much requested feature, I reckon.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
